<node name="ppcc_reg_ext"                         size="0xfc.0" descr="" >
	<field name="cmd_type"                        offset="0x0.0"    size="0x0.8" access="OP" descr="0x0 - get algo info0x1 - enable algo0x2 - disable algo0x3 - get algo enabling status0x4 - get num of params0x5 - get param info0x6 - get param0x7 - get &amp; clear param0x8 - set param0xA - bulk get. Reserved when method = Set0xB - bulk set. Reserved when method = Get0xC - bulk get counters. Reserved when method = Set0xD - bulk get and clear counters0xE - get num of counters. Reserved when method = Set0xF - get counter info. Reserved when method = Set0x10 - get algo info array0x11 - get algo slot counter group IDs0x12 - get histogram IDs for algo slot0x13 - histogram get description0x14 - histogram get0x15 - histogram set0xF0 - get supported target apps0xFF - reset params to default [Internal]" />
	<field name="lp_msb"                          offset="0x0.12"   size="0x0.2" access="INDEX" descr="Local port number [9:8]" />
	<field name="pnat"                            offset="0x0.14"   size="0x0.2" access="INDEX" descr="Port number access type. Determines the way local_port is interpreted:0 - Local port number1 - IB port number" />
	<field name="local_port"                      offset="0x0.16"   size="0x0.8" access="INDEX" descr="local_port number" />
	<field name="target_app"                      offset="0x0.28"   size="0x0.4" access="INDEX" enum="PCC_RP=0x0,PCC_NP=0x1,MULTIPATH=0x2" descr="0:PCC_RP1: PCC_NP2: MULTIPATH" />
	<field name="algo_slot"                       offset="0x4.0"    size="0x0.4" access="INDEX" descr="For command types other than 0x10 (get algo info array), must point to a\;present algo slot (a slot index with a non-zero algo id - as returned\;via Command type 0x10)For cmd_type = 0x12 (get histogram IDs for algo slot): Algorithm slot\;number - inputFor cmd_type = 0x13, 0x14, 0x15 (histogram commands): Histogram ID" />
	<field name="algo_param_index"                offset="0x4.16"   size="0x0.16" access="INDEX" descr="Selects the specific param or counter to get/set (if applicable, 0 if\;not). Index is zero-based. Must be smaller than value returned in\;get_num_of_params / get_num_of_counters.Appliccable for commands 0x5-0x8, 0xA-0xD.For cmd_type = 0x14 (histogram get): Histogram mode (output): 0 =\;LINEAR, 1 = EXPONENTIAL, etc.For cmd_type = 0x15 (histogram set): Histogram mode (input): 0 = LINEAR,\;1 = EXPONENTIAL, etc." />
	<field name="value"                           offset="0x8.0"    size="0x4.0" access="RW" descr="The layout of this field varies based on command type:For cmd_type = 0x0: returns 32-bit algo_num or 0 if no algo is available\;at this indexFor cmd_type = 0x3: returns 1 if enabled, 0 otherwiseFor cmd_type = 0x4: returns num of params algo hasFor cmd_type = 0x6:: returns value of param (selected by param index)For cmd_type = 0x7: returns value of param (selected by param index) and\;clears paramFor cmd_type = 0x8: The value to write to param (selected by param\;index). Set by the user. Set command is silently ignored if value\;outside min..max values (comparison is unsigned) or if param permission\;is not read-write.For cmd_type = 0xE: returns the num of counters algo has.For cmd_type = 0x11 (get algo slot counter group IDs): return the number\;of counter groups belonging to this algo slotFor cmd_type = 0x12 (get histogram IDs for algo slot): Number of\;histogram IDs (output)For cmd_type = 0x14 (histogram get): Number of edges (output, 2-33,\;which means 1-32 bins). Enable status is returned in param_value1.For cmd_type = 0x15 (histogram set): If value = 0: disable histogram\;(stops updating bins, bins are not cleared). If value = 1: enable\;histogram (re-enable without changing parameters). If value = 2-33:\;number of edges (input, which means 1-32 bins) - set parameters and\;enable.For cmd_type = 0xF0: returns a bit mask of supported appsAll the rest: returns 0" />
	<field name="param_value1"                    offset="0xc.0"    size="0x4.0" access="RO" descr="For cmd_type = 0x5: return default value of paramFor cmd_type = 0xE: returns the max counter group ID available. Counter\;group IDs are 0-indexed, the max ID would be num_groups-1.For cmd_type = 0x14 (histogram get): Enable status: 0 = disabled, 1 =\;enabledReserved for other commands" />
	<field name="param_value2"                    offset="0x10.0"   size="0x4.0" access="RO" enum="type_not_reported=0x0,accumulate=0x1,min=0x2,max=0x3" descr="For cmd_type = 0x5: return min legal value of paramFor cmd_type = 0xF: counter type.0: type_not_reported1: accumulate2: min3: maxReserved for other commands" />
	<field name="param_value3"                    offset="0x14.0"   size="0x4.0" access="RO" descr="For cmd_type = 0x5: return max legal value of paramFor cmd_type = 0xF: return max legal value of counter; counter\;wraps-around to 0 when exceeding this valueReserved for other commands" />
	<field name="sl_bitmask"                      offset="0x18.0"   size="0x0.16" access="RW" descr="This field allows to apply to specific SLs based on the bitmask. When a\;bit is set, it’s index SL shall be configured." />
	<field name="prm"                             offset="0x1c.0"   size="0x0.2" access="RO" descr="When cmd_type = 0x5 / 0xF:0-param / counter is read-only1-param / counter is read-write2-param / counter is read-only but may also be accessed and cleared via\;“get &amp; clear” commandReserved for other commands" />
	<field name="sl_bitmask_support"              offset="0x1c.2"   size="0x0.1" access="RO" descr="Indicates whether the device supports sl_bitmask logic" />
	<field name="counter_en"                      offset="0x1c.3"   size="0x0.1" access="RW" descr="When set, enables PPC algorithm-specific counters, otherwise they are\;disabled.Each port supports multiple counter groups, up to the number returned by\;cmd_type=0xE.Each counter group is associated with a specific [algo_slot,\;sl_bitmask]." />
	<field name="trace_en"                        offset="0x1c.4"   size="0x0.1" access="RW" descr="when set, indicates algorithm trace mechanism is enabled. Else, trace is\;disabled" />
	<field name="text_length"                     offset="0x1c.8"   size="0x0.8" access="RW" descr="Length in bytes of text fieldValid when cmd_type = 0x0 / 0x5  /\;0xA/ 0xB/ 0xC/ 0xD/ 0xF/ 0x10 / 0x12 / 0x13 / 0x14 / 0x15Reserved for other commands" />
	<field name="counter_group_id"                offset="0x1c.16"  size="0x0.4" access="RW" descr="Counter Group ID associated with the algorithm slot or query command.The value must be in the range 0 to the value returned by cmd_type = 0xE\;(max counter group ID).For enable commands (cmd_type = 0x1):If cfg_counter_group_en set, this field assigns the counter group ID to\;the algo_slot.This field is only applicable if the counter_en bit is set; otherwise,\;counters are not enabled.For GET slot commands (cmd_type = 0x3): If the counter_en bit is set,\;this field returns the counter group ID assigned to that slot. If the\;counter_en bit is set to 0, this field is reserved.For GET commands (cmd_type = 0xC, 0xD):If cfg_counter_group_en is set, this field specifies which counter group\;to query.For cmd_type = 0x14 (histogram get): Counter Group ID (output, 0-14) -\;returns counter group assigned to histogram.For cmd_type = 0x15 (histogram set): Counter Group ID assigns counter\;group to histogram." />
	<field name="cfg_counter_group_en"            offset="0x1c.20"  size="0x0.1" access="OP" descr="Counter Group ID configuration enable.For enable commands (cmd_type = 0x1):When set (1): the user configures the counter group ID when enabling the\;algorithm slot (via PPCC).When clear (0): allows the user’s algorithm code to set the counter\;group ID or default (counter group 0).For GET commands (cmd_type = 0xC, 0xD):When set (1): use counter_group_id from this command register to specify\;which counter group to query.When clear (0): use counter_group_id from the algorithm slot header\;(backward compatible behavior)." />
	<field name="text"                            offset="0x20.0"   size="0xdc.0" access="RW" high_bound="54" low_bound="0" descr="The layout of this field varies based on command type:0x0: algo name, comma, algo description (ASCII\;string)0x5: param name, comma, param description (ASCII string)0xA: Array of 32 bits parameters, starting from parameter index 0 up to\;(text_len/4 -1)0xB: Array of 32 bits parameters, starting from parameter index 0 up to\;(text_len/4 -1)0xC: Array of 32 bits counters, starting from parameter index 0 up to\;(text_len/4 -1)0xD: Array of 32 bits counters, starting from parameter index 0 up to\;(text_len/4 -1)0xF: counter name, comma, counter description (ASCII string)0x10: array of 32bit Algo info, up to 16 entries, representing which\;algo id is present per slot. Zero value means algo id is irrelevant.Algo Info: algo_id[31:16], algo_major_ver[15:8] algo_minor_ver[7:0]0x11 (get algo slot counter group IDs): Array of 32-bit counter group\;IDs (output). text[0] is the default (main) counter group for the slot;\;text[1] through text[value-1] are the other counter group IDs belonging\;to this slot (order is unspecified). The number of valid 32-bit entries\;equals value. text_length = value × 4 bytes.0x12 (get histogram IDs for algo slot): Array of 32-bit histogram ID\;values (output).text[0..N-1] contains the histogram ID array, where text[0] is the first\;histogram ID, text[1] is the second histogram ID, etc.The number of valid entries is indicated by value (number of histogram\;IDs).0x13 (histogram get description): Description string (output,\;null-terminated ASCII, up to 220 bytes). text[0..54] contains\;description string starting at offset 0.0x14 (histogram get): Array of 32-bit edge values (output). Only first\;num_edges entries are used (where num_edges is returned in value\;register).0x15 (histogram set): Array of 32-bit edge values (input). Only first\;num_edges entries are used (where num_edges is specified in value\;register).All commands are limited by text_len" />
</node>

